# A wiki repo only ever tracks: raw/, wiki/, and the top-level docs.
# Everything below is local/runtime junk that must never enter a wiki repo —
# a single `git add -A` sweeping a runtime tree in is what produced a 1,000-file
# pack and an HTTP 500 on push. Keep this list ahead of that failure mode.

# Editor / OS
.obsidian/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.stackdump

# Dev / language toolchains (any level)
node_modules/
.venv/
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env
.env.*
*.log

# Stray runtime/app/install trees that have ended up beside wiki content
# (root-anchored so a legitimately-named wiki page is never hidden)
/comfy/
/ComfyUI/
/models/
/output/
/input/
/temp/
/tmp/
/pip-cache/
/.cache/
